## Claim it first

Before doing any work, run:

    nat start-slice 3b738308-f654-8170-8c99-eccab4463d8f --project 3b738308-f654-8117-9f2e-c3b0a9b7f001

That claims the slice for Craig Johnston and prints your brief: the slice's own
body and acceptance criteria, followed by the project's conventions.
If it refuses — the slice is already claimed, or already done — stop and
say so rather than working the slice anyway.

Every `nat` command below names the project this slice is in:

    --project 3b738308-f654-8117-9f2e-c3b0a9b7f001

Put it on any other one you run too. Without it a command acts on
whatever project the user's board is on, which they can switch while
you work — and your writes would land in a plan you were never
launched on.

